+# Aegis — Safe Training & Annotation Patch
+
+This patch implements tooling to mitigate these pilot risks:
+
+- Overfitting to local conditions:
+  - services/simulation/domain_randomization.py: generate randomized synthetic scenarios for robust training and simulation.
+  - services/model/cross_validation.py: k-fold CV runner with MLflow logging to validate models against varied data.
+  - services/federated/federated_cv.py: prototype federated CV orchestration (clients run local CV and central aggregator aggregates metrics).
+
+- Data quality & annotation gaps:
+  - services/active_learning/milvus_sampler.py: Milvus-backed sampler storing embeddings and uncertainty metadata.
+  - services/annotation/active_loop_api.py: annotation Flask API to fetch top-K uncertain samples and submit annotations (integrates with Milvus).
+  - Active learning flow: compute embedding + uncertainty in training/eval loop (not included here — add model-specific adapter).
+
+- Athlete privacy / consent backlash:
+  - services/consent/consent_manager_optout.py: enhanced consent manager with opt-out and explainability request endpoints.
+  - Ensure any training pipeline checks consent opt-out flags and excludes opted-out subjects from datasets or federated aggregation.
+
+- Dependence on technology during competition:
+  - services/a2a/hil_approval.py: human-in-the-loop approval service to gate critical actions; signs and records evidence on approval.
+  - services/evidence/sign_and_record_decision.py: helper to sign decisions and send evidence to MCP / Rekor.
+  - Use fetchtoken / offline approvals (existing services/fetch) and edge sync_retry tooling (existing patch) for offline resilience.
+
+- Ethical / federation rules (equipment changes):
+  - Evidence signing ensures every equipment change or model recommendation has an auditable signed receipt.
